Chapter: WebWidgets
  cites UI chapter Widget

Section: Constructors

  wk-attach : WidgetNode, List WidgetNode, Integer, Integer -> WidgetNode
  wk-attach (w) (cs) (i) (n) =
    if i >= n then w
    else wk-attach (widget-add-child w (list-at cs i)) cs (i + 1) n
  widget-box : Text, Text, List WidgetNode -> WidgetNode
  widget-box (id) (cls) (children) =
    wk-attach (widget-custom id ("box:" & cls) 0 0) children 0 (list-length children)
  widget-box-click : Text, Text, List WidgetNode -> WidgetNode
  widget-box-click (id) (cls) (children) =
    wk-attach (widget-custom id ("boxc:" & cls) 0 0) children 0 (list-length children)

Section: Ids

 id-num reads the decimal number an element id ends with, supporting
 any number of trailing digits. An id with no trailing digit gives 0,
 therefore guard calls with a text-starts-with prefix check when 0 is
 a meaningful index. The digit range is anchored on the code of "0"
 rather than a numeric literal because the same source compiles
 against two encodings: CCE on bare metal (digits 3-12) and Unicode
 under the HTML plug (digits 48-57). Both are contiguous.

  id-num : Text -> Integer
  id-num (id) = id-num-loop id (text-length id - 1) 1 0
  id-num-loop : Text, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  id-num-loop (id) (i) (place) (acc) =
    if i < 0 then acc
    else let z = char-code-at "0" 0
    in let c = char-code-at id i
    in if c >= z & c <= z + 9 then id-num-loop id (i - 1) (place * 10) (acc + (c - z) * place)
    else acc

Section: Handlers

  no-pick : Text, Integer -> Integer
  no-pick (g) (i) = 0
